<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Position-Dependent Feature Contributions</h2>

<figure id="A3.F7" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.01251v1/progressive_window_all.svg" id="A3.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:381/254;" width="381" height="254"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>Spearman correlation with PE when training on a progressive window of tokens spanning the concatenated <span id="A3.F7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Postilla</span> and <span id="A3.F7.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Generated</span> segments. The vertical dashed line marks the boundary between the two segments.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Figure <a href="#S4.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ Detecting Low-Accuracy Answers ‣ 4.4 Q1 and Q2: Uncertainty Estimates Assessment ‣ 4 Experimental Evaluation ‣ Efficient Uncertainty Estimation for LLM-based Entity Linking in Tabular Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> reveals that performance differs depending on whether features are extracted from the <span id="A3.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Postilla</span> or <span id="A3.p1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Generated</span> tokens. To investigate this further, we designed an experiment that progressively expands a sliding window over the concatenated <span id="A3.p1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Postilla</span> and <span id="A3.p1.1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Generated</span> segments, measuring how information accumulates as more tokens are included. We evaluate three feature configurations: (1) output-layer features, (2) LogitLens features from intermediate layers, and (3) their combination. Figure <a href="#A3.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ Appendix C Position-Dependent Feature Contributions ‣ Efficient Uncertainty Estimation for LLM-based Entity Linking in Tabular Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> shows the Spearman correlation between each configuration and the baseline PE as a function of the window size. Correlation increases gradually while the window traverses the <span id="A3.p1.1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Postilla</span> tokens, with a pronounced jump once the <span id="A3.p1.1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Generated</span> tokens are reached. The improvement over <span id="A3.p1.1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Postilla</span> is non-uniform: certain positions—especially the final tokens—contribute disproportionately, indicating that the informative signal is unevenly distributed. Additionally, LogitLens features provide a benefit within the <span id="A3.p1.1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Postilla</span> segment but not after entering the <span id="A3.p1.1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Generated</span> portion, suggesting that during generation, the output-layer features already capture sufficient information, whereas intermediate-layer representations are more useful prior to generation. These observations imply that feature selection should be adapted based on token origin and position to maximize effectiveness. This also motivates extensions that localize uncertainty at the answer-bearing token(s), enabling per-token confidences and finer-grained handling of multi-answer outputs.</span></p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Spearman Correlation Between Estimated and True PE/SE</h2>

<figure id="A4.F8" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.01251v1/predicted_vs_true_PE_correlation.svg" id="A4.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:419/205;" width="419" height="205"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 8: </span>Spearman’s rank correlation coefficient (<math id="A4.F8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>) between the estimated entropy (PE or SE) and the multiple-generations entropy (PE or SE) across models. In the legend, the notation “<span id="A4.F8.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Target(Segment, Observable)</span>” indicates that the target variable <span id="A4.F8.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Target</span> was predicted using a regressor based on <span id="A4.F8.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Observable</span> features extracted from the <span id="A4.F8.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Segment</span> segment of the prompt.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Answer Variability as a Function of Temperature</h2>

<figure id="A5.F9" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.01251v1/temperature_sensitivity.svg" id="A5.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:452/154;" width="452" height="154"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 9: </span>Sensitivity to temperature of prompts with no output variation (<span id="A5.F9.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">red</span>), prompts with correct answers only – still no output variation (<span id="A5.F9.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">green</span>), and prompts with correct answer on average (<math id="A5.F9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq 0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq 0.5</annotation></semantics></math>, <span id="A5.F9.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">yellow</span>), <span id="A5.F9.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(left)</span> Gemma-2-9b-it, <span id="A5.F9.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(center)</span> Gemma-2-2b-it, and <span id="A5.F9.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(right)</span> TableLlama.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To evaluate the variability of answers and recoverable cases, we systematically sweep temperature values in the range <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.0\leq\tau\leq 2.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>2.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.0\leq\tau\leq 2.0</annotation></semantics></math> with steps of <math id="A5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1</annotation></semantics></math> to assess the temperature effect on (1) the number of items that show output variability and (2) the average accuracy. For capacity reasons, we utilize a subset of 200 elements from the original dataset.
Figure <a href="#A5.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ Appendix E Answer Variability as a Function of Temperature ‣ Efficient Uncertainty Estimation for LLM-based Entity Linking in Tabular Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> shows the results of the experiment for two selected LLMs. The <span id="A5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">yellow</span> series shows average accuracy, highlighting how higher <math id="A5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> values deteriorate the performance on the task. At the same time, lower <math id="A5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> settings yield the highest proportion of always correct cases (<span id="A5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">green</span> line). However, again at low <math id="A5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, output variability is also lowest; the uncertainty of these cases cannot be estimated, making this setting unsuitable for recovery. Operationally, a reasonable trade-off for <math id="A5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> is to minimize the accuracy loss while maximizing the number of cases recoverable through uncertainty, that is, those above the <span id="A5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">red</span> line. Another way to view this trade-off is by examining the difference between the <span id="A5.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">red</span> and <span id="A5.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">green</span> lines: this difference represents the proportion of unrecoverable cases, that is, cases that are always wrong and have no output variability. Making these cases recoverable requires “paying” by reducing always correct cases, while trying to preserve average accuracy (<span id="A5.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">yellow</span>) as much as possible. This experiment illustrates how temperature can be adjusted depending on specific combinations of model, task, and application constraints.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Transformer-Based Time Complexity</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To further assess the practicality and usability of our approach, in this section we derive the time complexity of a Transformer-based architecture, such as the ones used by the models considered in this work. We consider a Transformer with <math id="A6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> layers, and <math id="A6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> hidden size. The context length is set to <math id="A6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, while the number of generated tokens is <math id="A6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>. The time complexity of a single forward pass over a prompt <math id="A6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>can be decomposed into the following components:</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A6.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A6.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Self-attention:</span> Given the <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q,K,V\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q,K,V\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> matrices, the time complexity of the self-attention mechanism is <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(N^{2}\cdot d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(N^{2}\cdot d)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> is the context length and <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> is the hidden size. The attention scores are computed as <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="QK^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">QK^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the output is computed as <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(QK^{T})V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(QK^{T})V</annotation></semantics></math>. The time complexity of this operation is <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(N^{2}\cdot d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(N^{2}\cdot d)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Feed-forward:</span> During the feed-forward step, the time complexity is <math id="A6.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(8N\cdot d^{2})=O(N\cdot d^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(8N\cdot d^{2})=O(N\cdot d^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> overall, where <math id="A6.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> is the hidden size. In this we can include also the projection of the input to the <math id="A6.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="QKV" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">QKV</annotation></semantics></math> space and the final projection to the output space.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A6.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In total one has a time complexity of <math id="A6.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(N^{2}\cdot d+N\cdot d^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(N^{2}\cdot d+N\cdot d^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> for a single Transformer layer, which becomes <math id="A6.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(L[N^{2}\cdot d+N\cdot d^{2}])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(L[N^{2}\cdot d+N\cdot d^{2}])</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A6.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of layers.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p4.1" class="ltx_p">If we now suppose to generate <math id="A6.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> tokens without the use of a KV-cache, the time complexity of the <math id="A6.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>-th generation step is <math id="A6.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(L[(N+g)^{2}\cdot d+(N+g)\cdot d^{2}])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(L[(N+g)^{2}\cdot d+(N+g)\cdot d^{2}])</annotation></semantics></math>, for every <math id="A6.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in[G]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in[G]</annotation></semantics></math>. If we then sum over all the generations, we have:</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A6.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle O\left(\sum_{g=1}^{G}L\left[(N+g)^{2}d+(N+g)d^{2}\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle O\left(\sum_{g=1}^{G}L\left[(N+g)^{2}d+(N+g)d^{2}\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle O\left(L\sum_{g=1}^{G}\left[(N+g)^{2}d+(N+g)d^{2}\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle O\left(L\sum_{g=1}^{G}\left[(N+g)^{2}d+(N+g)d^{2}\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle O\left(L\sum_{g=1}^{G}\left[(N^{2}+2Ng+g^{2})d+(N+g)d^{2}\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle O\left(L\sum_{g=1}^{G}\left[(N^{2}+2Ng+g^{2})d+(N+g)d^{2}\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle O\left(L\left[(GN^{2}+2NG^{2}+G^{3})d+(GN+G^{2})d^{2}\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle O\left(L\left[(GN^{2}+2NG^{2}+G^{3})d+(GN+G^{2})d^{2}\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle O\left(L\left[G(N+G)^{2}d+G(N+G)d^{2}\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle O\left(L\left[G(N+G)^{2}d+G(N+G)d^{2}\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle O\left(LG\left[(N+G)^{2}d+(N+G)d^{2}\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle O\left(LG\left[(N+G)^{2}d+(N+G)d^{2}\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="2"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p6.1" class="ltx_p">which shows that the time complexity of generating <math id="A6.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> tokens is quadratic in the number of overall tokens <math id="A6.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N+G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N+G</annotation></semantics></math>, when <math id="A6.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\ll N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\ll N</annotation></semantics></math>, otherwise it would become cubic in the number of generated ones.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p7.1" class="ltx_p">When a KV-cache is used, while the time for processing the prompt is the same, a major computational saving is obtained during the generation phase. In this case, the time complexity of the <math id="A6.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>-th generation step can be decomposed into the following components:</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p8" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A6.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A6.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Self-attention:</span> During the self-attention, <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> reduces to a single vector <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{g}\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{g}\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, while <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K,V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K,V</annotation></semantics></math> becomes <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{g},V_{g}\in\mathbb{R}^{(N+g-1)\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{g},V_{g}\in\mathbb{R}^{(N+g-1)\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Overall, the time complexity of this operation is <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O((N+g)\cdot d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O((N+g)\cdot d)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Feed-forward:</span> Since the output of the Self-Attention has a dimension of <math id="A6.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times d</annotation></semantics></math>, the feed-forward step has a time complexity of this operation is <math id="A6.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(d^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(d^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, which includes the projection of the input to the <math id="A6.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="QKV" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">QKV</annotation></semantics></math> space and the final projection to the output space.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A6.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.p9.1" class="ltx_p">If we then sum over all the generations <math id="A6.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in[G]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in[G]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p10" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A6.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle O\left(\sum_{g=1}^{G}L\left[(N+g)d+d^{2}\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle O\left(\sum_{g=1}^{G}L\left[(N+g)d+d^{2}\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle O\left(L\sum_{g=1}^{G}\left[(N+g)d+d^{2}\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle O\left(L\sum_{g=1}^{G}\left[(N+g)d+d^{2}\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle O\left(L\left[G(N+G)d+Gd^{2}\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle O\left(L\left[G(N+G)d+Gd^{2}\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle O\left(LG\left[(N+G)d+d^{2}\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle O\left(LG\left[(N+G)d+d^{2}\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.p11.1" class="ltx_p">which shows that the time complexity of generating <math id="A6.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> tokens is linear in the number of overall tokens <math id="A6.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N+G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N+G</annotation></semantics></math>, when <math id="A6.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\ll N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\ll N</annotation></semantics></math>, otherwise it would become quadratic in the number of generated ones.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>Time complexity of the Transformer-based architecture. <math id="A6.T2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of layers, <math id="A6.T2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of tokens in the prompt, <math id="A6.T2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of generated tokens, and <math id="A6.T2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> is the hidden size.</figcaption>
<table id="A6.T2.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A6.T2.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T2.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-bottom: 1.07639pt;padding-left:9.0pt;padding-right:9.0pt;"><span id="A6.T2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Phase</span></td>
<td id="A6.T2.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-bottom: 1.07639pt;padding-left:9.0pt;padding-right:9.0pt;"><span id="A6.T2.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Without KV-cache</span></td>
<td id="A6.T2.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-bottom: 1.07639pt;padding-left:9.0pt;padding-right:9.0pt;"><span id="A6.T2.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">With KV-cache</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T2.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T2.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:9.0pt;padding-right:9.0pt;">Prompt processing</td>
<td id="A6.T2.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:9.0pt;padding-right:9.0pt;"><math id="A6.T2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(L[N^{2}\cdot d+N\cdot d^{2}])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(L[N^{2}\cdot d+N\cdot d^{2}])</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.T2.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:9.0pt;padding-right:9.0pt;"><math id="A6.T2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(L[N^{2}\cdot d+N\cdot d^{2}])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(L[N^{2}\cdot d+N\cdot d^{2}])</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T2.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T2.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-bottom: 1.07639pt;padding-left:9.0pt;padding-right:9.0pt;">Generation</td>
<td id="A6.T2.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-bottom: 1.07639pt;padding-left:9.0pt;padding-right:9.0pt;"><math id="A6.T2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(LG[(N+G)^{2}d+(N+G)d^{2}])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(LG[(N+G)^{2}d+(N+G)d^{2}])</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.T2.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-bottom: 1.07639pt;padding-left:9.0pt;padding-right:9.0pt;"><math id="A6.T2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(LG[(N+G)d+d^{2}])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(LG[(N+G)d+d^{2}])</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="A6.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p12.1" class="ltx_p">This simple derivation shows that our proposed approach to learn to estimate the multiple-generations Predictive Entropy (PE) is still computationally promising even when advanced KV-cache techniques are employed during inference.</p>
</div>
</section>
